<%- include('../../partials/policy-start') %>
<p class="lead">This policy explains what we collect when you take the 100% online Food Handler Certification course, why, and how we protect it. Questions: <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>
<h2>What we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account details</strong>: your name (printed on your certificate), email address and a securely hashed password. We never store your password itself.</li>
  <li><strong>Learning records</strong>: lessons completed, time spent on lessons, exam answers and scores.</li>
  <li><strong>Final exam proctoring</strong>: before the exam, a photo of you, a photo of your government ID and a short video of your room. During the exam, your camera and microphone are on, and we take periodic camera snapshots. We also record your IP address, browser type and events such as leaving the exam page, another person in view or a second screen. Face detection runs inside your browser; no images are sent to any other company.</li>
  <li><strong>Payment status</strong>, if a course is paid. Card details are handled by our payment processor and never touch our servers.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Why we use it</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To run your account, track your progress and issue your certificate.</li>
  <li>To let employers confirm a certificate is genuine. The public verification page shows only the certificate number, your name, the course and its dates.</li>
  <li>To keep the platform secure and prevent cheating and fraud.</li>
</ul>
<h2>How proctoring data is protected</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Photos, videos and snapshots are encrypted before they are stored, each with a key bound to your exam.</li>
  <li>Only authorised staff can view them. Identity reviewers see your exam evidence and nothing else, and every view is logged.</li>
  <li>They are deleted automatically <%= locals.decisionDays || 30 %> days after your exam is decided, and never kept longer than <%= locals.retentionDays || 90 %> days.</li>
  <li>They are used only to confirm your identity and that the exam was taken under the required conditions — never for marketing, and never sold or shared.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Service providers</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Hosting and database:</strong> your account, learning records and encrypted exam evidence are stored in Canada.</li>
  <li><strong>Email delivery:</strong> account and exam emails (your name, email address and reference codes, never ID images) are sent through Resend, which processes them in the United States.</li>
  <li><strong>Course videos:</strong> chapter videos are streamed by Bunny.net. The video player receives your IP address and browser details, as any website does, but no account information.</li>
  <li><strong>Payments:</strong> card payments are handled by Stripe.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Your choices</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>See your data:</strong> download everything we hold about you from your account page (<em>Download my data</em>).</li>
  <li><strong>Correct it:</strong> update your details on your account page, or email us if your name is already on a certificate.</li>
  <li><strong>Delete it:</strong> delete your account from your account page at any time. Your profile, progress and exam recordings are erased. A certificate already issued stays verifiable by its number (name, course and dates only) until it expires, because employers rely on it.</li>
  <li><strong>Security alerts:</strong> we email you when your password or two-step verification changes.</li>
</ul>
<p>Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>
<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>We use one essential cookie to keep you signed in. We don't use advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
<%- include('../../partials/policy-end') %>
